# F94 machinery control (INTENT 11.214) - no body, no table lookup.
# `struct if` with a literal that is always true.  If THIS one does not answer
# 2037, the instrument is broken and nothing measured with it means anything;
# it isolates "struct if / date / readback works" from "the table is wrong".
# Observable: the clock, read back through the shipped `get status position`
# (field 4 = JDay).  2037-01-01 = the branch fired, 2038-01-01 = the else fired,
# 2030-01-01 = neither (the play never reached the test).
timerate rate 0
date utc 2030-01-01T00:00:00
wait duration 1
struct if 1 equal 1
date utc 2037-01-01T00:00:00
struct if else
date utc 2038-01-01T00:00:00
struct if end
